import LeanMlir.Proofs.Foundation.IntervalBoundConv

/-! # IBP `L∞` scorecard for a CONVOLUTIONAL net — generated instance

The first certificate in this repo that covers a convolution, a max-pool, and
more than two layers. Generated by `scripts/ibp_conv_scorecard.py`; the engine
is `IntervalBoundConv.lean` (`BoxSound3`/`BoxSound3V`, `ibp3_certified_of_boxSound`).

Net (trained, then rationalized to `k/256` — the QUANTIZED net is what is
certified, so the certified network is the deployed one):

  `conv2d(4 out-channels, 3×3 SAME) → reluT → maxPool2 → denseT(4·4·4 → 10)`

Input: MNIST zero-padded 28×28 → 32×32, 4×4 average-pooled to 8×8, exact
`k/4080` pixel rationals. Quantized test accuracy **0.8256**.

Perturbation model: pixel `L∞`, `∀ a b d, |δ a b d| ≤ ε`, at ε = 1/255, 2/255,
4/255, 8/255 — the same grid as the dense `LipschitzCertScorecardIBP.lean`, so
the two tiers are directly comparable. A pooled coordinate is an AVERAGE of 16
raw pixels, so a radius-ε `L∞` ball on the raw image maps into the radius-ε ball
on the pooled image: these radii keep their literature meaning.

Per image the certificate is a real theorem — `CertifiedAtLinf3 net ε x y`, i.e.
`∀ δ, (∀ a b d, |δ| ≤ ε) → ∀ j ≠ y, net (x+δ) j < net (x+δ) y` — not a numeric
report. Counts are LOWER bounds: a loose box cannot prove an image
UNcertifiable. All `propext / Classical.choice / Quot.sound`. -/

